OL,3,C'We're with Ukraine until they win',
OL,4,Csays defence secretary on visit to Kyiv
OL,6,FJuly marked the deadliest month for
OL,7,FUkrainian civilian casualties since
OL,8,Fthe war began, according to the Kyiv
OL,9,Fgovernment.
OL,11,FThe rate and scale of Russian missile
OL,12,Fstrikes on Ukrainian cities has been
OL,13,Fexacerbated by a shortage of missile
OL,14,Fdefence systems.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G4/12
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,000,100
PN,31705
SC,0005
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F317A1786018700
OL,3,C'We're with Ukraine until they win',
OL,4,Csays defence secretary on visit to Kyiv
OL,6,F"What I'm going to do is to understand
OL,7,Fwhat more we can do to support Ukraine
OL,8,Fthrough what will be a challenging
OL,9,Fwinter, but also beyond, because
OL,10,Fultimately it's in our national
OL,11,Finterest as well as, you know, the I
OL,12,Fthink the collective and moral good
OL,13,Ffor Ukraine to win," Streeting said.
OL,15,FBoth Russia and Ukraine do not publish
OL,16,Ffigures for military casualties caused
OL,17,Fby the war, but the loss of life on
OL,18,Fthe Russian side is thought to be in
OL,19,Fthe hundreds of thousands.
OL,26,@nD@AOU
